{"id":15470,"date":"2025-10-30T14:33:35","date_gmt":"2025-10-30T14:33:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/?p=15470"},"modified":"2026-07-29T05:55:22","modified_gmt":"2026-07-29T05:55:22","slug":"7-ps-of-marketing","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/7-ps-of-marketing\/","title":{"rendered":"7 P\u2019s of Marketing Mix: Elements, Examples, Importance"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>Ever wondered why brands like McDonald\u2019s, Apple, or Coca-Cola are recognized and loved everywhere? It\u2019s because they master not just one aspect of marketing but all of them together: product, pricing, promotion, people, and more. These combined elements form what is known as the marketing mix.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Earlier, marketers followed only the 4 Ps of marketing mix, which included Product, Price, Place, and Promotion. Over time, three more were added: People, Process, and Physical Evidence. Together they form the 7 Ps of Marketing, a proven framework to plan, execute, and measure any business strategy.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Let\u2019s understand the 7 Ps of marketing mix in simple terms with examples you can relate to.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Are the 7 P\u2019s in Marketing?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The 7 Ps of Marketing are seven key elements that help a company meet customer needs and build long-term satisfaction.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>These are:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><\/td><td><strong>Element<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Meaning<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Product<\/td><td>What you sell<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td>Price<\/td><td>What customers pay<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>Place<\/td><td>Where customers find it<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>Promotion<\/td><td>How people learn about it<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>5<\/td><td>People<\/td><td>Everyone involved in delivering it<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td>Process<\/td><td>How it\u20